  "interpretation": [
    "Every outcome/residual scalar parameter changed and every private critic parameter advanced 1,560 Adam steps across 60 updates. Updating does not imply better calibrated predictions.",
    "Complete labels exist for all transitions, but 8,192 draws with replacement are reused across two epochs. Unique transition and opening coverage are about 54 percent; omission is uniform sampling, not the old future-dependent label-selection bias.",
    "Transition weighting gives longer games more representation. This is not automatically bias in an on-policy conditional-value estimator; game-weighted evaluation and state-occupancy training use different measures.",
    "The residual target detaches terminal_value, blocking direct outcome-tower gradients, but both critic losses still reach the shared encoder. Synthetic gradients prove routing, not harmful interference in the trained model.",
    "Most steps undergo global gradient clipping. This does not establish insufficient learning: direction, shared losses and Adam scaling matter.",
    "Zero probability-floor hits in these evaluation forecasts do not exclude rare floor hits in training."
  ],
